{
  "entries": [
    {
      "abstract": "For every C > 0 and every N there exist n ≥ N and an n-point set P ⊆ ℝ² whose number of unit-distance pairs exceeds n^(1 + C / log log n). This refutes Erdős's 1946 conjectured bound ν(n) ≤ n^(1 + C/log log n) for an absolute constant C. The theorem quantifies over C > 0; this is harmless because any bound with C ≤ 0 would imply the corresponding bound for a positive C.\n",
